+sources: [.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md, .harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md, 3556e27, bee6a4d, claude/hooks/conductor-gate.sh, tests/gate-denied.list]
+verified_by: tests/gate.test.sh
+---
+# 0012: Gate shrink (prune step 5)
+
+**Context.** Prune step 5 of [0011](0011-single-runner-headless.md) asked for a smaller conductor gate. The analyst plan (`.harness/gate-shrink-detail.md`, 2026-10-28) replayed 881 conductor Bash calls through the gate: 754 allowed, 127 denied. Never used: `git show --stat`, `herdr status`, `pane list|layout`, `workspace|tab list`, `gh issue|run|repo|auth|browse|pr status`, jq as a pipe consumer. Chaining was 44 of 754 (5.8%), pipes 0, `2>&1` 0. The gate was 552 lines. The B′ spike (native subagents instead of the harness runner) was rejected on 2026-11-03 (`.harness/spike-bprime/RESULTS.md`): subagents die on conductor exit ("1 local agent couldn't be moved and was stopped") and the report reaches the conductor before verify finishes. The runner stays, so the gate stays and is trimmed, not replaced.
+
+**Decision.** Trim to observed usage and keep the core:
+- Done earlier, in `3556e27` (gate v21) and the agent_type change: one-command scanner replaces the segment splitter; jq allowlist, `git_branch_ok`, `show`, most `gh` groups and the `herdr` extras are gone; `Agent|Workflow|Monitor|NotebookEdit` are denied by `disallowedTools` in `claude/agents/conductor.md` and the matcher is `Edit|Write|Read|Grep|Glob|Bash`; the gate keys on `agent_type`; `tests/gate-denied.list` is the regression list. Gate is now 513 lines.
+- Done here: the `--via` no-op arm is removed from `ask_parse_args` (`--via` is now an unknown option, exit 1). The policy tables (`BASH_ALLOW`, `GH_ALLOW`, `GIT_DENY`, messages) already sit in one block after the prologue, so no move was needed.
+- Kept: the path helpers (`rel`, `physrel`, `physical`, readable/writable, raw-stream): they are the symlink and raw-stream protection and cannot shrink to a 50-line gate. The Bash allowlist stays because `harness`, `gh pr`, read-only `git`, `cat`/`ls` are what the conductor really runs.
+- Rejected (option f): replace the gate with `permissions` rules. User-scope rules also bind workers (same settings file), deny beats allow so "deny Read except .harness/docs" cannot be written, and Bash patterns are fragile. Only tool-name denies are possible, and `disallowedTools` already covers those.
+
+**Status.** Active. Supersedes the "4b" consequence in [0005](0005-gate-only-inside-herdr.md).
+
+**Consequences.** Conductor shell is one simple command per call (see the troubleshooting page `conductor-shell-one-command`). A filesystem MCP server added later is not covered by the gate (none configured). Gate edits stay live: `bash -n` and `tests/gate.test.sh` before each save ([live-gate-edit](../troubleshooting/live-gate-edit.md)).
